- `ADD_TEST KitWindowModelTests`
- `ADD_TEST KitWindowTests`

**How to implement.** The kit window shows its kit: an opened kit carries its folder, and the window's title names the kit, its folder, whether it is read-only and the constructor (001 §O 'the title shows the kit name and folder'; the S5.3 brief: read-only shows in the title; step 155: S5.3 adds the title marker). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitOpening.fs`: `OpenedKit` (step 150) gains `folder : KitFolder` as its first field, documented in one line: the folder the kit was opened from. The private `openedOver` (step 172) takes `(folder : KitFolder)` first and sets it; `openKitAt` and `openExistingKitAt` pass the folder they opened; `withRebindings` keeps it. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`. `TableAndElementRotationModel` gains, after `kit` (step 152), `kitFolderOpt : KitFolder option`, documented in one line: the kit's folder, `None` for the scratch kit of a scene that opened no folder. `initWith` sets it to `None`; `loadKit` (step 152) sets it to `Some opened.folder`. On the `type TableAndElementRotationModel with` extension that holds `loadKit`, each documented in one to three lines citing spec 0050 S5.3: `member model.kitCaption : ControlCaption` is the kit's name (`model.kit.kitFile.name`), then ` (read-only)` when `model.kit.access` is `ReadOnlyKitAccess`, then ` — ` and the folder's text when `kitFolderOpt` is `Some`; and `member model.kitWindowTitle : ControlCaption` is `kitCaption`, ` — Optical Constructor — ` and `Main` for `ForwardConstructor` or `Inverse` for `InverseConstructor`, the words the launcher's buttons use. So a read-write kit `Optics QZ` in `C:/kits/Optics QZ` is titled `Optics QZ — C:/kits/Optics QZ — Optical Constructor — Main`; opened read-only, `Optics QZ (read-only) — C:/kits/Optics QZ — Optical Constructor — Main`; and the scratch kit `Scratch kit — Optical Constructor — Main`. (3) `OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs`, `ConstructorScene.mount` (`Program.fs:71`): the view it runs sets `window.Title <- model.kitWindowTitle.value` and then answers `mainView model dispatch`, so the title follows the model on every change (a mode switch, step 186; a reload's new name, step 187). `MainConstructorWindow` and `InverseConstructorWindow` delete their literal titles (`Program.fs:94`, `:112`), and their docs say the title names the kit. No title setting, format option or cache is added. Tests. `OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitOpeningTests.fs` (step 150) gains `an opened kit carries the folder it was opened from`: `openKitAt` read-write and read-only and `openExistingKitAt` (step 172), over one folder each, answer an opened kit whose `folder` is that folder; each is closed at the end. New `OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs`, `module KitWindowModelTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of the compile list with no comment. Its folders are GUID-named under `Path.Combine(System.AppContext.BaseDirectory, "KitWindowModelTests")`; a kit named `Optics QZ` is made in a folder of that name inside one through `KitOpening.openKitAt` read-write with `ClockProvider.system`, `KitAuthor "test"` and an import context over `BuiltinCatalogue.freshStores ()` (step 94), as `KitOpeningTests` makes its kits; a fact's model is `initMain ()` loaded with `loadKit` of the opened kit; every kit a fact opens is closed at its end. `the window title names the kit, its folder and the constructor`: the loaded model is titled `Optics QZ — <the folder's text> — Optical Constructor — Main`, and with `constructorMode = InverseConstructor` it ends `— Inverse`. `a kit opened read-only is marked in the title`: the kit closed and opened again with `ReadOnlyKitAccess` titles the model `Optics QZ (read-only) — <the folder's text> — Optical Constructor — Main`. `a scene that opened no folder is titled by its kit alone`: `initMain ()` is titled `Scratch kit — Optical Constructor — Main`. New `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs`, `module KitWindowTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests`, appended at the end of the compile list with no comment, gains, without a trait, `a constructor window is titled by its kit`: `MainConstructorWindow(ctx, opened)` over `TestAppScope.freshAppContext (FolderName "KitWindowTests")` and `TestAppScope.openedKitIn (FolderName "KitWindowTests") ctx.catalogueImports` (step 152), shown headless, is titled `<the kit's name> — <its folder's text> — Optical Constructor — Main`, and `InverseConstructorWindow` over a second such kit ends `— Inverse`; both windows are closed, which releases their kits (step 154). Every other fact that builds a constructor window keeps its code and its assertions.

**Acceptance.** After the title lands, `OpenedKit.folder` MUST name the folder a kit was opened from, and a constructor window's title MUST be its model's `kitWindowTitle`, naming the kit, `(read-only)` for a kit opened read-only, the folder and the constructor; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `an opened kit carries the folder it was opened from`, `the window title names the kit, its folder and the constructor`, `a kit opened read-only is marked in the title` and `a scene that opened no folder is titled by its kit alone`, the count rising by 4; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `a constructor window is titled by its kit`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the fourteen s21 invariants MUST pass.
